        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "19fc5841-059d-51f1-bda0-0186577d8b5d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vinko Knežević\n- Places: County of Tyrol, Graz, Marengo\n- Organizations: Habsburg Monarchy, Austrian Empire, Holy Roman Empire, Austria-Hungary\n- Roles: Croatian nobleman, general\n- Events: Battle of Marengo\n\nFacts:\n- The County of Tyrol was established about 1140 as a state of the Holy Roman Empire.\n- In 1804, the Princely County of Tyrol was unified with the secularised Prince-Bishoprics of Trent and Brixen and became a crown land of the Austrian Empire.\n- Vinko Knežević was born on 30 November 1755 and was a Croatian nobleman and general in the imperial army service of the Habsburg Monarchy.\n- Vinko Knežević commanded an infantry brigade at Marengo the following year.\n- In 1805, Vinko Knežević led Austrian Empire troops in the Tyrol.\n- In 1809, Vinko Knežević led Austrian Empire troops at Graz.\n- From 1867, the County of Tyrol was a Cisleithanian crown land of Austria-Hungary.\n- Vinko Knežević died on 11 March 1832.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
